          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.086,
            0.848,
            0.128
          ],
          "content": "？ Give some possible scores for Krishita in the three rounds so that they add up to give $2 3 p - 7 q .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.145,
            0.677,
            0.169
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Can we say who scored more? Can you explain why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.176,
            0.848,
            0.236
          ],
          "content": "How much more has Krishita scored than Charu? This can be found by finding the difference between the two scores. $2 3 p - 7 q - ( 2 1 p - 9 q )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.241,
            0.475,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": "Simplify this expression further."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.283,
            0.626,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": "**Example 9:** Simplify the expression $4 \\left( x + y \\right) - y$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.309,
            0.821,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": "Using the distributive property, this expression can be simplified to"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.378,
            0.334,
            0.619,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}4\\left(x+y\\right)&-y=4x+4y-y\\\\&=4x+4y+-y\\\\&=4x+(4-1)y\\\\&=4x+3y.\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.457,
            0.849,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": "**Example 10:** Are the expressions 5u and $5 + u$ equal to each other? The expression 5u means 5 times the number $u ,$ and the expression $5 ~ + ~ u$ means 5 more than the number u. These two being different operations, they should give different values for most values of u."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.549,
            0.328,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": "Let us check this."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.588,
            0.848,
            0.63
          ],
          "content": "？ Fill the blanks below by replacing the letter-numbers by numbers; an example is shown. Then compare the values that 5u and $5 + u$ take."
        },
        {
